WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:06.399
Professor Sycamore's Pokémon summer camp is off and running

2
00:00:06.466 --> 00:00:09.700
and our heroes have wasted no time making new friends,

3
00:00:09.766 --> 00:00:12.666
Trainers Tierno, Shauna and Trevor.

4
00:00:12.733 --> 00:00:16.833
With their Pokémon at their sides, all three have dreams of success

5
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.800
but just what kind of influence those dreams

6
00:00:18.866 --> 00:00:21.933
will have on our heroes is yet to be seen.

7
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.766
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

8
00:00:24.833 --> 00:00:28.333
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

9
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.066
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

10
00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:34.233
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

11
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.300
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

12
00:00:37.366 --> 00:00:40.500
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

13
00:00:40.566 --> 00:00:43.933
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

14
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.366
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

15
00:00:46.433 --> 00:00:48.866
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

16
00:00:48.933 --> 00:00:51.933
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon! ♪

17
00:01:11.466 --> 00:01:13.000
Clemont, come on, hurry!

18
00:01:15.433 --> 00:01:19.500
- Serena's not fooling around, is she?
- That's because she's super-excited

19
00:01:19.566 --> 00:01:23.433
about all the cool stuff we're going to be doing in camp today!

20
00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:28.033
Right! We can do it! Today's the day we get those ten points!

21
00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.100
- Yeah!
- You're going to get left behind!

22
00:01:43.666 --> 00:01:48.199
- Good morning, Professor. You're up early.
- Good morning, Nurse Joy.

23
00:01:48.266 --> 00:01:52.199
That was quite a day yesterday. This year's campers are all very unique!

24
00:01:52.266 --> 00:01:54.500
We had a few surprises, didn't we?

25
00:01:54.566 --> 00:01:57.333
Yes. The fishing competition was wild!

26
00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:14.000
Yeah, Team Squirtle ended up with quite a catch and they did it in a creative way.

27
00:02:14.066 --> 00:02:16.799
They earned every one of those ten points.

28
00:02:16.866 --> 00:02:18.700
Today should be just as fun!

29
00:02:18.766 --> 00:02:21.933
Yes, I'm sure it will be a marvelous day, indeed.

30
00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.133
Delicious! Mm.

31
00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.566
It's a little bit unusual, but it tastes great!

32
00:02:30.633 --> 00:02:34.433
- Yeah! What do you think, Pikachu?
- Pika! Pikachu!

33
00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:40.866
Mm. I've never tasted anything like this. You can really taste the ingredients.

34
00:02:40.933 --> 00:02:42.900
I wonder what this is.

35
00:02:44.866 --> 00:02:49.933
- It's really, really good!
- Delightful. I'm swelling with pride!

36
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.799
Ha! Even if we were to get fired from Team Rocket, we'd still land on our feet!

37
00:02:54.866 --> 00:02:59.433
You just keep your eyes on the prize! We're here to steal Pokémon for the Boss!

38
00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:01.866
- You!
- Ma'am!

39
00:03:04.799 --> 00:03:06.566
Such exquisite meals!

40
00:03:06.633 --> 00:03:10.299
Maybe I should give you a raise.

41
00:03:10.366 --> 00:03:12.000
Thank you!

42
00:03:13.233 --> 00:03:16.366
- Good morning, campers!
- Good morning!

43
00:03:17.866 --> 00:03:21.366
What a lovely day. It's perfect summer camp weather!

44
00:03:21.433 --> 00:03:25.566
Today, you'll all be making your own PokéVision videos!

45
00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:30.266
- Its PokéVision time!
- I want in, too.

46
00:03:30.333 --> 00:03:34.433
- Why don't you go in by yourself?
- Wobbuffet!

47
00:03:35.399 --> 00:03:39.066
I'm pretty sure some of you have made PokéVision videos before.

48
00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:42.966
But just in case, it refers to making a Pokémon promo video.

49
00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:46.166
I'd like to show a video that I made as an example.

50
00:03:48.666 --> 00:03:52.166
Hi there! Welcome to the Sycamore Pokémon Lab.

51
00:03:52.233 --> 00:03:55.100
This is where I spend my time researching

52
00:03:55.166 --> 00:03:59.266
and taking good care of your first Pokémon partners.

53
00:03:59.333 --> 00:04:03.833
And that's not all. My assistants and I are also busy conducting daily research

54
00:04:03.899 --> 00:04:06.066
on Pokémon Evolution.

55
00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:10.833
The more we research, the more we find in the world of Pokémon!

56
00:04:10.899 --> 00:04:13.500
They're all truly amazing!

57
00:04:14.899 --> 00:04:18.033
If you have any questions about the world of Pokémon,

58
00:04:18.099 --> 00:04:21.766
don't hesitate to get in touch!

59
00:04:24.133 --> 00:04:28.466
Thank you. Thanks so much. I'm really grateful for your generous applause.

60
00:04:28.533 --> 00:04:29.766
Thanks.

61
00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:34.800
As you just saw, PokéVision lets Trainers and Pokémon

62
00:04:34.866 --> 00:04:38.233
show what makes them special to an even wider audience.

63
00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:43.633
And so, for today, each team is going to make their very own PokéVision video.

64
00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:46.166
Now, to help you make exciting videos,

65
00:04:46.233 --> 00:04:50.333
I've got all the tools you need to make Poké Puffs. Please put them to good use!

66
00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:53.766
- Ah.
- Awesome! What should I make?

67
00:04:53.833 --> 00:04:56.599
- Serena, what are you going to do?
- Hm.

68
00:04:56.666 --> 00:05:00.099
- I have to think!
- I want to make some too!

69
00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:04.266
All right, campers, I'd like you to finish your videos by this evening.

70
00:05:04.333 --> 00:05:06.900
As always, the top three teams earn points!

71
00:05:06.966 --> 00:05:11.099
This will be decided by a vote we will take right here after the big screening.

72
00:05:15.333 --> 00:05:18.233
I'm expecting to see some great work!

73
00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:20.466
Ready? Begin!

74
00:05:24.599 --> 00:05:27.800
Perfect. I've been wanting to do another video.

75
00:05:27.866 --> 00:05:30.666
No one's going to beat me today!

76
00:05:30.733 --> 00:05:32.700
Yeah. No one's going to beat me!

77
00:05:32.766 --> 00:05:36.933
There's no doubt Shauna's got this whole PokéVision thing in the bag,

78
00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.666
which means we'll be extending our lead.

79
00:05:39.733 --> 00:05:44.366
Nope, no way! We're going to make a PokéVision video you won't believe!

80
00:05:44.433 --> 00:05:47.066
- Pika! Pikachu!
- Let's win, Serena!

81
00:05:52.866 --> 00:05:57.800
Ta-da! Here's the concept! It's called Friends!

82
00:05:57.866 --> 00:05:59.700
- Pika?
- Na-na-na?

83
00:05:59.766 --> 00:06:01.599
Those are our Pokémon?

84
00:06:01.666 --> 00:06:04.466
Yup. The five of them are our stars!

85
00:06:04.533 --> 00:06:08.000
- Dedenne, can you handle it?
- Na-na!

86
00:06:08.066 --> 00:06:12.500
You'll be great. The only thing you have to do is be yourself!

87
00:06:12.566 --> 00:06:16.033
And I'll be in charge of making beautiful Poké Puffs.

88
00:06:16.099 --> 00:06:20.200
- All right! We can't lose!
- Yes! Let's aim for the top!

89
00:06:20.266 --> 00:06:22.933
We'll take everything we learned during our journey

90
00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:26.000
and put it all in our PokéVision video. It's going to be great!

91
00:06:26.066 --> 00:06:27.500
Yeah!

92
00:06:27.566 --> 00:06:30.166
I've learned from my past mistakes.

93
00:06:30.233 --> 00:06:34.466
Of course, that means the future is now, thanks to science!

94
00:06:34.533 --> 00:06:36.566
Clemontic Gear on!

95
00:06:36.633 --> 00:06:38.799
Revised and better than ever,

96
00:06:38.866 --> 00:06:42.000
my latest invention, the Pokéstar Shooter Mark Two!

97
00:06:42.066 --> 00:06:45.266
Ash, I still need to make some minor adjustments,

98
00:06:45.333 --> 00:06:48.466
- so would you please assist me?
- Sure. No prob!

99
00:06:55.533 --> 00:06:59.933
Fennekin! Kin! Kin!

100
00:07:02.733 --> 00:07:04.633
This is kind of hard.

101
00:07:05.633 --> 00:07:08.166
- There!
- Ah. So cute!

102
00:07:08.233 --> 00:07:10.700
Fennekin, do you think it's cute too?

103
00:07:10.766 --> 00:07:13.666
Isn't it the sweetest? Fennekin, just a sec.

104
00:07:13.733 --> 00:07:16.866
- Fenn!
- Let's make some more of these cuties!

105
00:07:16.933 --> 00:07:19.566
- Okay!
- Hey, Serena?

106
00:07:19.633 --> 00:07:22.566
Did you see Aria's newest PokéVision video yet?

107
00:07:22.633 --> 00:07:25.633
Huh? So Aria has a new video?

108
00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:27.566
No, I haven't had a chance to.

109
00:07:27.633 --> 00:07:31.066
It's got a lot of style! You've just got to see it!

110
00:07:31.133 --> 00:07:34.566
Aria's Fennekin evolved into Braixen!

111
00:07:36.866 --> 00:07:39.466
That's wonderful news! A Braixen!

112
00:07:39.533 --> 00:07:43.200
Isn't it great? She's an awesome Trainer. Listen to this.

113
00:07:43.266 --> 00:07:46.733
She got super-super popular after becoming a Pokémon performer,

114
00:07:46.799 --> 00:07:50.966
but she still insists on regularly putting out new PokéVision videos!

115
00:07:51.033 --> 00:07:54.700
- Performer?
- You don't know what that is?

116
00:07:54.766 --> 00:07:56.533
No. Tell me!

117
00:07:56.599 --> 00:07:59.466
Pokémon performers are made up of the cutest Trainers.

118
00:07:59.533 --> 00:08:03.099
They even have their own Pokémon Performer Festival!

119
00:08:03.166 --> 00:08:05.733
Ever heard of the Pokétacular?

120
00:08:05.799 --> 00:08:08.599
No, we've never heard of that either.

121
00:08:08.666 --> 00:08:11.166
Uh! Wow. I guess you don't know anything!

122
00:08:11.233 --> 00:08:12.599
Let's see, okay.

123
00:08:12.666 --> 00:08:18.099
The Pokétacular is a performance event that takes place all over Kalos

124
00:08:18.166 --> 00:08:21.166
and the cute and talented Trainers who participate in it

125
00:08:21.233 --> 00:08:23.533
are called Pokémon performers!

126
00:08:25.166 --> 00:08:29.099
The Pokétacular is made up of two competitions.

127
00:08:29.166 --> 00:08:31.333
The first one is called the Theme Performance,

128
00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:36.100
making Poké Puffs, grooming Pokémon, performing with props, things like that.

129
00:08:36.166 --> 00:08:38.466
And sometimes there will be special theme programs,

130
00:08:38.533 --> 00:08:42.033
depending on the specific competition.

131
00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:49.566
The second one is called General Freestyle Performance. See?

132
00:08:49.633 --> 00:08:52.466
You have to use your Pokémon's skills to their fullest

133
00:08:52.533 --> 00:08:55.900
and the Pokémon appears on stage along with its Trainer!

134
00:09:02.933 --> 00:09:05.233
If you're good enough to win three or more competitions,

135
00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:08.800
then you get to appear in what's called the Master Class!

136
00:09:08.866 --> 00:09:11.900
And the Trainer who wins there along with her Pokémon

137
00:09:11.966 --> 00:09:15.100
gets to receive the title of Kalos Queen!

138
00:09:16.933 --> 00:09:20.866
And who's the Kalos Queen now? It's none other than Aria!

139
00:09:20.933 --> 00:09:25.466
Kalos Queen. Wow! Doesn't that sound totally amazing?

140
00:09:25.533 --> 00:09:28.199
Mm-hm, but it doesn't sound like you battle.

141
00:09:28.266 --> 00:09:32.500
That's right. Pokémon performance demonstrates the partnership between

142
00:09:32.566 --> 00:09:35.900
Pokémon and Trainer in a completely different way than having a battle.

143
00:09:35.966 --> 00:09:37.699
You want to be a performer?

144
00:09:37.766 --> 00:09:41.266
I sure do. Right now I'm researching with style!

145
00:09:41.333 --> 00:09:46.800
I'll work real hard, then enter a competition and fulfil my dream!

146
00:09:46.866 --> 00:09:48.433
Being Kalos Queen!

147
00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:51.433
- Serena. Bonnie.
- Huh?

148
00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:54.033
- Sorry we're late.
- Pika, pika!

149
00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:55.433
Are you ready to go?

150
00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:57.933
I'll be all ready in just a sec!

151
00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.500
Who's that Pokémon?

152
00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.366
It's Bulbasaur!

153
00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:15.800
- Time for location scouting!
- Uh, what's that?

154
00:10:15.866 --> 00:10:18.033
Finding the best place to shoot the video!

155
00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:19.566
Oh, right.

156
00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:26.033
I think we're getting pretty far away from camp.

157
00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:30.800
If we go a little further, I think we might find the perfect spot!

158
00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:36.300
Come on. We're going to end up spending the whole day searching.

159
00:10:36.366 --> 00:10:38.666
Yeah. Maybe you're right.

160
00:10:38.733 --> 00:10:40.199
Now what?

161
00:10:40.266 --> 00:10:41.933
-Pika!

162
00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.300
There! How does that look?

163
00:10:44.366 --> 00:10:48.500
It's the best place I've seen so far, with all those flowers blooming!

164
00:10:48.566 --> 00:10:50.300
Wait, Serena!

165
00:10:50.366 --> 00:10:53.966
I'll just have a quick look and then we can start!

166
00:10:58.266 --> 00:11:00.633
Ah! Ash!

167
00:11:00.699 --> 00:11:01.966
Serena!

168
00:11:08.333 --> 00:11:11.000
Ash, are you okay?

169
00:11:11.066 --> 00:11:14.566
- Yeah! How about you?
- I'm all right.

170
00:11:14.633 --> 00:11:18.966
- Pikachu!
- Hey there, buddy. It's good to see you.

171
00:11:19.033 --> 00:11:21.866
- Here.
- Huh?

172
00:11:21.933 --> 00:11:23.533
Thank you very much, Ash.

173
00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:25.966
- Oh!
- Ash!

174
00:11:26.033 --> 00:11:30.466
- Pika! Pi!
- Ah. Must've twisted it a little.

175
00:11:30.533 --> 00:11:32.966
Hm. No big deal. I'm fine.

176
00:11:33.033 --> 00:11:37.566
- I'm sorry, it's my fault.
- No, it's okay.

177
00:11:37.633 --> 00:11:38.966
- Hey!
- Huh?

178
00:11:39.033 --> 00:11:42.166
Hey, Ash and Serena, are you all right?

179
00:11:42.233 --> 00:11:45.800
- Yeah! Don't worry. We're fine!
- Pikachu!

180
00:11:45.866 --> 00:11:48.400
No. Ash hurt his foot and can't walk!

181
00:11:48.466 --> 00:11:52.466
Understood! Serena, you stay there with Ash!

182
00:11:52.533 --> 00:11:53.900
We'll go get help!

183
00:12:03.966 --> 00:12:06.733
Ash, I feel so awful about this.

184
00:12:07.866 --> 00:12:09.866
I'm fine!

185
00:12:11.866 --> 00:12:15.000
Okay. The swelling should go down a bit now.

186
00:12:15.066 --> 00:12:17.733
That's nice of you, Serena!

187
00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:20.500
And thanks for worrying about me too Pikachu!

188
00:12:20.566 --> 00:12:23.900
- Pika! Pikachu!
- Pikachu is so awesome.

189
00:12:23.966 --> 00:12:26.900
Coming to find you because it cares so much about you.

190
00:12:26.966 --> 00:12:31.233
Pikachu and I have been in a lot of tough spots together, that's for sure.

191
00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:32.566
Pikachu.

192
00:12:32.633 --> 00:12:36.333
- Long as we're a team, we're fine!
- Pika! Pika!

193
00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:39.400
Okay, Fennekin, come out!

194
00:12:39.466 --> 00:12:41.400
Fenn! Fennekin! Fenn!

195
00:12:41.466 --> 00:12:45.733
Ah! We're always a team, too!

196
00:12:47.633 --> 00:12:49.099
Hungry?

197
00:12:49.166 --> 00:12:51.166
- Here you go.
- Fenn!

198
00:12:57.199 --> 00:12:59.966
- So they're both all right?
- Yeah!

199
00:13:00.099 --> 00:13:03.599
Ash hurt his foot a bit, but it sounded like he was okay.

200
00:13:03.666 --> 00:13:08.066
That's good. We'll put together a rescue team right away.

201
00:13:08.133 --> 00:13:10.966
Hope they're all right. I'm worried.

202
00:13:13.466 --> 00:13:16.233
Of course we still have the PokéVision video to do.

203
00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:20.400
- Right!
- You know, we've done a lot at camp!

204
00:13:20.466 --> 00:13:23.466
And when I'm battling, I'll be able to use it all.

205
00:13:23.533 --> 00:13:28.066
Wow, even the fishing contest? That's going to help you battle, too?

206
00:13:28.133 --> 00:13:31.633
Yeah, you bet! Nothing we ever do is a waste of time!

207
00:13:31.699 --> 00:13:35.233
Everything on our journey leads to the Kalos League!

208
00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:38.099
That's why the more stuff we do the better!

209
00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:44.099
You're always doing your best. And you've done so much.

210
00:13:44.166 --> 00:13:49.833
But I'm not done yet. After all, I've got to make my dream come true!

211
00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:52.199
And that dream is?

212
00:13:52.266 --> 00:13:54.333
To become a Pokémon Master!

213
00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:58.666
Of course. You really are an amazing person.

214
00:14:00.733 --> 00:14:04.400
- Let me get some more water.
- Thanks!

215
00:14:06.933 --> 00:14:10.599
A dream. Having a dream.

216
00:14:10.666 --> 00:14:12.833
Serena, are you okay?

217
00:14:17.533 --> 00:14:23.333
Sometimes I wonder, what is my dream, Ash? What is it that I want?

218
00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:26.866
Don't worry! You've got lots of time to figure out your dream!

219
00:14:26.933 --> 00:14:32.333
- Pika!
- Fenn! Fenn! Fennekin!

220
00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:34.699
- Fennekin!
- Fenn!

221
00:14:34.766 --> 00:14:37.699
I'll bet you find your dream together with Fennekin!

222
00:14:37.766 --> 00:14:40.066
- Pika! Pikachu!
- Right?

223
00:14:40.133 --> 00:14:44.533
- Pika!
- I'll find my dream with my Pokémon.

224
00:14:46.266 --> 00:14:48.733
- Hello?
- Huh?

225
00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:51.333
Sounds like Professor Sycamore!

226
00:14:51.400 --> 00:14:55.433
- There you are. Are you all right?
- Yeah! We're fine!

227
00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:58.566
The rescue team's on its way down now!

228
00:14:58.633 --> 00:15:02.000
- Got it!
- Thanks, Professor!

229
00:15:04.233 --> 00:15:08.333
Well, we'll give those twerps a bit of a break just this one time.

230
00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:10.000
But nothing's changed!

231
00:15:10.066 --> 00:15:13.000
We've still got our evil eyes on the prize!

232
00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:16.866
We're here! You can all rest easy now.

233
00:15:16.933 --> 00:15:19.466
- You'll be back at camp in a jif!
- Huh!

234
00:15:19.533 --> 00:15:21.199
Hey, thanks!

235
00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:25.866
- Sorry to put you through all that.
- Fret not!

236
00:15:25.933 --> 00:15:28.099
That was nice of you to get us out.

237
00:15:28.166 --> 00:15:31.400
We really didn't mean to cause any trouble, Professor.

238
00:15:31.466 --> 00:15:34.366
I'm just glad it was nothing serious.

239
00:15:38.233 --> 00:15:40.066
It's beautiful!

240
00:15:42.733 --> 00:15:46.099
- Man, would you look at this place.
- Pika!

241
00:15:46.166 --> 00:15:49.866
And it was waiting for us right off the main path!

242
00:15:49.933 --> 00:15:53.266
This is a great spot. Time for PokéVision!

243
00:15:53.333 --> 00:15:54.366
Na-na-na-na!

244
00:15:54.433 --> 00:15:57.033
It's perfect! After all we've been through,

245
00:15:57.099 --> 00:15:59.366
we'll make the best PokéVision video ever!

246
00:16:08.333 --> 00:16:12.466
All right! Now for our next video from Team Squirtle!

247
00:16:12.533 --> 00:16:17.400
Hey! We're Team Squirtle! Allow me to introduce the tricked-out trio

248
00:16:17.466 --> 00:16:20.833
that's taken the Pokémon summer camp by storm!

249
00:16:22.466 --> 00:16:25.833
The super-speed battling Charmander!

250
00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:26.900
Char!

251
00:16:26.966 --> 00:16:30.900
And when it comes to Pokémon knowledge, I'm second to none. Trevor!

252
00:16:30.966 --> 00:16:32.366
Squirtle! Squirtle...

253
00:16:32.433 --> 00:16:35.533
Battling's all about moving and grooving for Squirtle!

254
00:16:35.599 --> 00:16:38.633
And with pro dancing on my mind, I'm Tierno!

255
00:16:38.699 --> 00:16:43.099
No matter what's up, it's rock solid and reliable Bulbasaur!

256
00:16:46.300 --> 00:16:51.300
With dreams of being a Pokémon performer dancing in my head, I'm Shauna!

257
00:16:51.366 --> 00:16:55.266
Team Squirtle's always on the prowl for battling opponents!

258
00:16:55.333 --> 00:16:57.000
Thank you all so very much!

259
00:16:57.066 --> 00:17:00.266
We tried everything we could do to bring out the best in our Pokémon!

260
00:17:00.333 --> 00:17:02.466
Thanks to all of you for your support!

261
00:17:02.533 --> 00:17:04.833
Wow, you were great, Team Squirtle!

262
00:17:04.899 --> 00:17:07.366
Yeah, what an amazing PokéVision video!

263
00:17:07.433 --> 00:17:09.866
- Next up, Team Froakie!
- Huh.

264
00:17:09.933 --> 00:17:12.133
This is our last PokéVision video!

265
00:17:13.399 --> 00:17:16.066
- Oh!
- Don't you still have work to do?

266
00:17:16.133 --> 00:17:17.633
Ma'am!

267
00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:24.599
Presenting something I made myself in front of all these people.

268
00:17:24.666 --> 00:17:26.599
I'm so nervous.

269
00:17:33.633 --> 00:17:37.600
I'm Serena and this is my partner, Fennekin!

270
00:17:37.666 --> 00:17:39.200
Kinn!

271
00:17:39.266 --> 00:17:43.366
Today, we're having a picnic, so I've made a basket of Poké Puffs.

272
00:17:43.433 --> 00:17:46.066
- Fennekin loves them!
- Fennekin!

273
00:17:46.133 --> 00:17:49.066
What have I done? I'm so sorry, Fennekin!

274
00:17:49.133 --> 00:17:52.066
Somebody grab the runaway Poké Puff!

275
00:17:56.533 --> 00:18:00.100
Pin! Che!

276
00:18:00.166 --> 00:18:04.566
-Che!

277
00:18:04.633 --> 00:18:10.600
Oh, well! Here! I've got enough for everyone!

278
00:18:17.600 --> 00:18:21.100
- Thank you so much, everybody!
- Yeah, thanks a lot!

279
00:18:22.766 --> 00:18:24.100
Oh, wow!

280
00:18:24.166 --> 00:18:26.933
So now that we've seen everyone's video,

281
00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:30.566
I want you all to pick the three videos you liked the most,

282
00:18:30.633 --> 00:18:32.666
other than your own, of course.

283
00:18:36.533 --> 00:18:40.933
The idea for using Poké Puffs in our video came from what we went through today.

284
00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:42.800
Huh. No joke?

285
00:18:42.866 --> 00:18:44.333
Hm. Nope!

286
00:18:44.399 --> 00:18:49.533
Today, Ash said there's nothing we could ever do that's a waste of time.

287
00:18:51.300 --> 00:18:54.000
That Ash is a pretty smart guy!

288
00:18:56.133 --> 00:19:01.133
You know, it would be beyond amazing if I could go and see a Pokétacular sometime

289
00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:03.966
and see what a Pokémon performer does, too!

290
00:19:04.033 --> 00:19:06.866
- Then I'll go with you!
- Ah! Sure!

291
00:19:08.333 --> 00:19:11.033
Come in, guys! They're announcing the winners!

292
00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:12.899
Pika!

293
00:19:12.966 --> 00:19:16.100
Okay! Thanks! Let's go!

294
00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:20.600
Thanks to your votes, we've decided on the top three PokéVision videos

295
00:19:20.666 --> 00:19:22.600
and the third place goes to...

296
00:19:22.666 --> 00:19:23.966
Team Charmander!

297
00:19:24.033 --> 00:19:26.966
-Yeah! Awesome! All right!

298
00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:30.733
You all did a great job

299
00:19:30.800 --> 00:19:32.966
showcasing the unique beauty of Water types!

300
00:19:33.033 --> 00:19:36.466
- And now the second place team.
- And that's Team Chikorita!

301
00:19:40.133 --> 00:19:44.533
You showed the elegance of Flying types in a masterful way!

302
00:19:48.533 --> 00:19:50.866
Finally, we come to the winning team.

303
00:19:50.933 --> 00:19:53.399
And the first place goes to...

304
00:19:57.700 --> 00:19:59.366
Team Froakie!

305
00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:07.633
- Congratulations!
- Thanks so much!

306
00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:09.433
Guess that's the way it goes.

307
00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:12.933
It's possible we went a little too battle-crazy,

308
00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:16.933
but I don't mind losing to Ash and his friends that much.

309
00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:20.200
The way you brought out the unique character of each Pokémon,

310
00:20:20.266 --> 00:20:23.133
that is what put you over the top.

311
00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:26.866
So then all three winning teams will be receiving points.

312
00:20:26.933 --> 00:20:29.233
Congratulations! You should be proud.

313
00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:30.933
Great job today, everyone!

314
00:20:31.933 --> 00:20:34.233
Thanks to an unexpected turn of events,

315
00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:38.766
our heroes have succeeded in making a great first-place PokéVision video!

316
00:20:38.833 --> 00:20:43.233
That means Team Froakie and Team Squirtle are tied with the most points,

317
00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:46.666
as the summer camp adventures continue!
